Wave 2 invariants — locked by `src/test/safety/safetyPerfCapaWave2.test.ts`.

## Cache invalidation (POLICY §110 cache isolation)

Incident mutations in `useSafetyIncidents.ts` MUST NOT invalidate the bare
`['safety']` root. Doing so re-runs every Safety sub-module query (assets,
training, permits, audits, emergency, notifications, …) on every transition.

Allowed scoped keys per mutation:

- `useReportSafetyIncident` → `SAFETY_SLA_QUEUE_KEY`, `['safety','incidents','drill']`, `['safety','dashboard-stats']`, `['safety','audit-log']`.
- `useTransitionSafetyIncident` → above + `['safety','incident', incidentId]` + `['safety','incident-detail', incidentId]`.
- `useReviveOrphanedIncident` → same as transition.

The `invalidateAllSafetyQueries` helper has been removed; do NOT reintroduce
a generic broad-invalidator.

## Severity reorder

`useReorderSafetyIncidentSeverities` MUST use `Promise.all` (parallel
round-trips), not a sequential `for` loop. Reorder lists are bounded
(≤ ~12 items in practice) so a single RPC is unnecessary; the parallel
fetch already collapses latency from N×rtt to ~1×rtt.
